# Altitude — line-ending contract.
#
# The repo had none until now, so what landed in a working tree depended on
# each contributor's `core.autocrlf`. Every tracked text blob in the repo is
# already LF (verified), so this file changes nothing about what is stored —
# it only makes the behaviour explicit and machine-independent.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: let git detect text and normalize to LF on commit. Working-tree EOL
# stays platform-native (CRLF on Windows), which is what already happens under
# `core.autocrlf=true` — so adding this does not force a re-checkout.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts — LF in the WORKING TREE on every platform.
#
# Why these need `eol=lf` and the rest don't: their emitters write LF
# unconditionally (`JSON.stringify`, `lines.join('\n')`). With a native-EOL
# checkout the file on disk is CRLF, so every regeneration rewrites it as LF.
# The content hash is unchanged, but git's stat cache can never settle
# (`git status` shows " M" forever while `git diff` is empty — see
# `git status --porcelain=v2`, which prints the same blob hash on both sides).
# Pinning the checkout to LF makes generate → status a genuine no-op.
#
# This does NOT fix carriage returns that end up inside JSON *string values*
# (serialized as the escaped `\r` sequence). Those are file content, not line
# terminators, and git normalization cannot touch them — they are fixed in the
# emitters: `libs/al-web-components/cem-plugins/al-deterministic.mjs` and
# `scripts/generate-component-schemas.js`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libs/al-web-components/custom-elements.json                text eol=lf
libs/al-web-components/schemas/**                          text eol=lf
libs/al-web-components/components/icon/fonts/iconfont.css  text eol=lf
libs/al-web-components/components/icon/fonts/iconfont.svg  text eol=lf
.altitude/baselines/**/*.json                              text eol=lf
.altitude/ai-readiness/**/*.json                           text eol=lf
.altitude/golden-snapshots/*.expected                      text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute on Linux/macOS/CI.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are tool-written; keep them byte-stable across platforms.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never EOL-convert, never diff as text.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
